plicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TEIKOKU CHEMICAL INDUSTRIES CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISHIDE TOSHIKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OTSUKI TETSUYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKASHITA YOSHIAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SATOH MITSUNOBU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUENAGA HITOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIDE, TOSHIKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OTSUKI, TETSUYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKASHITA, YOSHIAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATOH, MITSUNOBU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUENAGA, HITOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Compositions for forming metal oxide films which contain an amine salt of a metal complex formed by a ligand having 5 or less coordination positions and a metal compound.  Compared with the conventional compositions containing an amine salt of a metal complex formed by a ligand having 6 or more coordination positions and a metal compound, such a composition can contain a metal oxide at an elevated concentration.  Owing to this high concentration, a uniform film having a relatively large thickness can be obtained by a single film-forming operation, which is advantageous from the viewpoint of the production process.  In addition, the transportation cost of the film composition can be largely reduced.  The ligand having 5 or less coordination positions to be used therein is excellent in biodegradability, which relieves environmental pollution in the production process</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne des compositions de formation de couches minces d'oxyde métallique contenant un sel aminé d'un complexe métallique constitué d'un ligand ayant cinq positions de coordination ou moins et d'un composé métallique. Comparé aux compositions classiques contenant un sel aminé d'un complexe métallique constitué d'un ligand ayant six positions de coordination ou davantage et d'un composé métallique, cette composition peut contenir un oxyde métallique à une concentration élevée. Du fait de cette concentration élevée, une couche mince uniforme ayant une épaisseur relativement grande peut être obtenue par une seule opération de formation de couche mince, laquelle est avantageuse du point de vue du processus de production. De plus, le coût de transport de la composition de couche mince peut être réduit sensiblement. Le ligand ayant cinq positions de coordination ou moins à utiliser dans ces compositions présente une excellente biodégradabilité, ce qui réduit la pollution de l'environnement liée au processus de production.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_l